      "skill_id": "en-a1-017",
      "title": "Short instructions and imperatives",
      "explanation": "An imperative gives an instruction and uses the base verb with no subject: Open your books. Listen to the teacher. For a negative instruction put Don't (or Do not) before the base verb: Don't talk in class. Add please to be polite: Open the door, please. The verb never takes -s or -ing in an imperative.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "Open your books."
        },
        {
          "en": "Don't talk, please."
        },
        {
          "en": "Listen to the teacher."
        }
      ],
