    {
      "skill_id": "en-a1-018",
      "title": "Joining ideas with and, but and or",
      "explanation": "And adds one idea to another: I like tea and coffee. But contrasts two ideas: I like tea, but I don't like coffee. Or offers a choice: Do you want tea or coffee? Put a comma before but when it joins two clauses. These connectors join words, phrases or clauses of the same kind.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I like tea and coffee."
        },
        {
          "en": "I like tea, but I don't like coffee."
        },
        {
          "en": "Do you want tea or coffee?"
        }
      ],
      "references": ["CAM-A1-YLE", "COE-CV20"],
