    {
      "skill_id": "en-a1-019",
      "title": "Have got for possession",
      "explanation": "Have got says what someone has: I have got a brother. She has got a new bike. Use have got with I, you, we and they and has got with he, she and it. Negative: haven't got, hasn't got. Questions put have or has first: Have you got a pen? Short answers repeat have or has: Yes, I have. No, she hasn't. The contracted forms I've got and she's got are common in speech.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I have got a brother."
        },
        {
          "en": "She has got a new bike."
        },
        {
          "en": "Have you got a pen?"
        }
      ],
