    {
      "skill_id": "en-a1-020",
      "title": "Can for ability and permission",
      "explanation": "Can is a modal verb. Use can plus the base verb for ability (I can swim) and can't (cannot) for inability (She can't drive). The form never changes: not She cans. Questions put can first: Can you swim? Short answers: Yes, I can. No, I can't. Can is also used to ask permission: Can I open the window? There is no do or does with can.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I can swim."
        },
        {
          "en": "She can't drive."
        },
        {
          "en": "Can I open the window?"
        }
      ],
      "references": ["CAM-A1-YLE", "BC-A1-A2"],
